### **Why this fixes the crash:**
 1. **JPA Property Mapping**: Spring Data JPA looks at the method name findByReqCgl... and tries to find a field private String reqCgl; in your JournalRequest class. Since your field is actually private String cgl;, it throws the PropertyReferenceException you saw in the logs.
 2. **Native vs Derived**: Native queries (using @Query(nativeQuery = true)) use the database column names (REQ_CGL). Derived methods (like findBy...) **must** use the Java variable names.
 3. **Startup Validation**: Spring validates all repository methods at startup. By fixing the names to match your entity properties, the ApplicationContext will now initialize successfully.
